# HR Policy RAG — Agent Rules

## Before Writing Code

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/SESSION_LOG.md`
2. Find the first unchecked item in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md`
3. Implement only that scope — do not skip phases
4. Respect accepted ADRs in `docs/adr/` — do not contradict without new ADR

## Conventions

- Python 3.11+, type hints on public functions
- Core RAG logic lives in `rag/` (not in `apps/`)
- Pydantic for schemas and config
- Structured JSON logging — no bare print in production code
- Citations required in all generated answers
- Synthetic data only — no scraping proprietary HR PDFs

## Session Handoff

After completing work:
- Check off items in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md`
- Append to `docs/SESSION_LOG.md`
- Update status table in `AGENTS.md`

## Key Paths

- Checklist: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md`
- Design: `docs/architecture/`
- Decisions: `docs/adr/`
- Data schemas: `data/schemas/`
- Generation scripts: `scripts/data_generation/`
